owner was away … flagged for review\" text is kept verbatim (at-most-one-Incident is still awaiting the owner's ruling); SS-3 and verdict #33 carry a superseded-by-0052 note that keeps the response (status, lead, severity, comms, write-up) PERMANENTLY OUT; SPEC §I.1.1 moves `incidents` to a row describing the grouping as IN and the response as OUT; CONTEXT.md's ⚠️ markers on Incident/Correlator/Conversation are removed and the bare word `incident` is no longer a scope ban. **The lint choice, stated:** `incident_id` stays banned **on signal rows** — the rule is narrowed to fire only where the column would sit on `alerts`, `alert_cases`, `notifications` or `notification_deliveries` (SCOPE-BOUNDARY §5.6's door), so the Incident membership table's foreign key is legal; a lintvocab test proves both directions (a migration adding `alert_cases.incident_id` fails; `incident_members.incident_id` passes). 0053 and 0054 stay Proposed. `just ci` green.\n\n**Blocked by.** None — can start immediately.\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}